Description: pick a concrete libsdl-dev provider in Build-Depends
 `debian/control` bare-lists `libsdl-dev` as a Build-Depends.  That
 name is a virtual package with two concrete providers in bookworm:
 .
   libsdl1.2-dev          1.2.15+dfsg2-8   (original SDL 1.2)
   libsdl1.2-compat-dev   1.2.60-1         (SDL1.2 ABI on top of SDL2)
 .
 When neither is already installed, `apt-get build-dep` refuses to
 disambiguate (see the `llvm-toolchain-15` patch for the longer
 explanation of why bookworm's apt is strict here):
 .
   E: Package 'libsdl-dev' has no installation candidate
 .
 Fix follows standard Debian practice for build-depending on a
 virtual: alternation with a concrete preference first.
 .
   libsdl1.2-dev | libsdl-dev
 .
 Choice of `libsdl1.2-dev` over `libsdl1.2-compat-dev`:
   * libde265 only needs SDL for a small display utility in `dec265`
     — the original SDL 1.2 ABI is sufficient.
   * libsdl1.2-dev pulls a smaller transitive closure (the compat
     variant pulls libsdl2-dev).
   * Matches the intent of the original bare `libsdl-dev`: any
     SDL 1.2 ABI provider is fine, prefer the original.
 .
 Keeping `| libsdl-dev` as the second alternative means a system
 that already has `libsdl1.2-compat-dev` installed by some other
 build still satisfies the build-dep without a second concrete
 install.
 .
 Surfaced during GROUPS-01 phase 3 gnome build 2026-05-15 — libde265
 is pulled in transitively (likely via gnome-shell → tracker →
 gstreamer-plugins-bad's HEVC decoder, which links libde265).
Author: Harkirat S Virk <harkiratsvirk@gmail.com>
Origin: local
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-05-15
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- a/debian/control
+++ b/debian/control
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@
 Build-Depends:
  debhelper-compat (= 13),
  qtbase5-dev | libqt4-dev,
- libsdl-dev,
+ libsdl1.2-dev | libsdl-dev,
  libswscale-dev,
  libx11-dev,
  libxext-dev,
